§ CSLv3 RESEARCH SYNTHESIS
I> reconciled: pasted (436-source compact), on-disk (full comparative analysis)
I> v3 merges both → actionable findings + design decisions

§ KEY FINDINGS BY TRACK

§§ T1: DENSE NOTATION SYSTEMS
  I> Iverson (APL, 1979 Turing): notation shapes cognition, ¬ just records it ★
  I> APL: 1 glyph = 1 op → dense but tokenizer-hostile in modern BPE ⚠
  I> J: ASCII fallback solves tokenizer → ADOPTED (dual-mode glyphs §01)
  I> Ithkuil: 96 morphological slots → too extreme for human
     → took slot-system principle w/ bounded slots (§03 morpheme stacking)
     → took silent-defaults principle (§02 slot omission)
     → took multi-channel encoding (position + nesting + delimiters)
  I> Lojban: unambiguous grammar via rigid word-classes → ADOPTED (§02 BNF)
     → attitudinal system → confidence markers orthogonal to content
  I> Sanskrit samasa: 4 compound types cover most composition → ADOPTED+1
     → v3 has 5 types: TP DV KD BV AV (§03)
     → Panini's Ashtadhyayi: grammar IS compression algorithm ★
     → information geometry: compound formation = natural-parameter encoding ★
  I> Egyptian determinatives: semantic type-markers w/o phonetics
     → ADOPTED as postfix suffixes 'd 'f 's + domain prefixes § ∫ ⊞ (§01)
  I> Peirce Existential Graphs: enclosure = negation, spatial = logical
     → PARTIAL ADOPT: indent=cut, adjacency=AND (§04)
     → full 2D impractical for text streams

§§ T2: COMPRESSION THEORY
  I> Shannon: EN ≈ 1.3 bpc; practice higher ∵ redundancy
     → EN spec content ≈ 75% redundant
  I> Kolmogorov: min-description-length uncomputable; BPE = usable proxy
  I> rate-distortion: spec compression = near-lossless domain
     → target d(x,x̂) = 0 on implementation-relevant info
     → accept loss on stylistic redundancy only
  I> information geometry (Amari): Fisher metric → optimal encoding follows
     natural parameter structure → MATCHES samasa intuition ★
  I> LLMLingua (Microsoft): 2-5× compression w/ minimal perplexity loss
     → 20× achievable w/ 1.5% accuracy loss on GSM8K
     → LLMs ¬ need EN grammar to reason; need semantic content
     → CSLv3 target (5-6×) = plausible, conservative

§§ T3: 2D/SPATIAL
  I> Penrose tensor diagrams: 2D saves complex index notation → USE (§04)
  I> Feynman: time-axis convention → USE in reason traces (§05)
  I> Befunge etc: full 2D syntax = pedagogical dead-end for serious use ✗
  I> structured editors (projectional): separate display from storage
     → FUTURE consideration for CSLv4

§§ T4: AI REASONING EFFICIENCY
  I> CoT compression: models CAN reason in compressed forms when prompted ✓
     → but drift toward verbose EN w/o reinforcement ⚠
  I> tokenizer matters HUGELY: single unicode glyph may = 3-5 BPE tokens
     → measure every glyph; ASCII aliases mandatory (§12)
  I> "Let's think step by step" → equivalent gain from dense structured
     reasoning (§05 trace format) ✓
  I> context window freed by compression = more simultaneous reasoning ★

§§ T5: PL THEORY
  I> concatenative (Forth/Factor): stack = implicit context
     → ADOPTED for pipeline ops |> <| (§01, §08)
  I> rank polymorphism (APL/J/Futhark): one fn, many shapes
     → ADOPTED (§07, §08)
  I> dependent types (Agda/Idris): types-as-specs
     → ADOPTED (§07)
  I> term rewriting: spec = executable
     → ASPIRATION for CSLv3 compiler v2

§ DESIGN DECISIONS (v3 reconciled)
  D1: dual-glyph-ASCII everywhere (J-style) ∵ tokenizer
  D2: 5 compound types (Sanskrit + Karmadhāraya) ∵ coverage w/o overload
  D3: postfix determinatives (Egyptian) ∵ optional annotation, low cost
  D4: rigid precedence (Lojban) ∵ unambiguous parse
  D5: morpheme-stack for modality (Ithkuil-lite) ∵ dense but bounded
  D6: Peircean indent = scope ∵ text-stream friendly linearization
  D7: 2D only for genuinely-2D data (tables, tensors, causal graphs)
  D8: ASCII-aliases W! specified per glyph (§12) ∵ fallback, editor support
  D9: tiered glyph inventory ∵ learnability (tier-0 < 2hr)
  D10: evidence markers orthogonal to content (Lojban attitudinals)
  D11: determinative suffixes as ASCII fallback for type markers
  D12: slot grammar w/ silent defaults (Ithkuil principle)

§ REJECTED (explored, ¬ adopted)
  ✗ full Ithkuil morphology ∵ unlearnable in <2hr
  ✗ pure 2D syntax (Befunge) ∵ incompatible w/ text streams
  ✗ color-channel encoding ∵ accessibility, medium-dependent
  ✗ >20 primitive glyphs for logic ∵ cognitive load
  ✗ Peirce Gamma (modal graphs) ∵ complexity > value
  ✗ Toki Pona minimalism ∵ extreme ambiguity = opposite of spec needs
  ✗ de Bruijn beyond 3 levels ∵ human readability degrades fast
  ✗ `>` for bahuvrihi (v2-specs) ∵ conflicts w/ comparison operator
  ✗ `°` for avyayibhava (v2-pasted) ∵ `@` more intuitive + ASCII-native

§ MULTI-CHANNEL ENCODING (from on-disk research §3)
  available channels in text:
  | channel            | capacity    | CSLv3 use                    |
  |--------------------|-------------|------------------------------|
  | glyph identity     | primary     | §01 glyph table              |
  | position (horiz)   | indent=scope| Peircean cut linearized       |
  | position (vert)    | sequence    | temporal/logical order        |
  | adjacency          | co-present  | juxtaposition = conjunction   |
  | nesting            | bracket depth| scope hierarchy              |
  | delimiter type     | category    | Egyptian determinatives       |
  | case               | UPPER/lower | ¬ used (reserved for future)  |
  | unicode block      | domain      | math/symbol = domain markers  |
  | whitespace pattern | binding     | dense = tight binding         |
∎
